WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.042
Retail devices are physical items owned by your shop.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:07.667
Start by choosing new or refurbished at the top.

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:12.083
Never create a retail record for a customer's repair device.

00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:18.375
Enter the category, brand and model, then copy identifiers from
the physical device.

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:22.625
Two devices of the same model still need separate records.

00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:28.250
Record memory, built-in storage and individual drives
separately where applicable.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.792
Leave unknown values empty, not zero.

00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:36.292
Do not infer this device's configuration from its product name.

00:00:36.292 --> 00:00:41.625
Next, record appearance, battery condition and supplied
accessories.

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:45.042
Known issues must belong to this device.

00:00:45.042 --> 00:00:50.958
Upload photos after creating the record, and never mark an
untested check as passed.

00:00:50.958 --> 00:00:54.542
Enter the asking price and storage location.

00:00:54.542 --> 00:00:57.500
Cost fields require permission.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.250
Confirm shop ownership using the checkbox, then create the
record.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.958
A new device remains awaiting inspection, not ready for sale.

00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:13.875
Record the actual inspection in the device details, then follow
the approval process to make it available.

00:01:13.875 --> 00:01:20.000
Sale, payments, handover and after-sales are recorded
separately for this same device.
